The full paper is only 14 pages and contains no proved hardness theorem. Its native candidates are the SAP witness \(A\) with \(AR=T\), or the DP witness \((A_1,A_2)\) with \(P=A_1XA_2\) in \(E_p^{(m)}\). Both are inverse-generatable and exactly checkable, but the paper’s security discussion is heuristic (mostly “few units”), so I’m now testing whether these equations collapse to routine modular linear algebra before deciding whether even Track B is honest.
