codex
Completed a verified Track B generator using the paper’s native \(E_p^{(n)}\) decomposition objects.

Key results:

- All G1–G9 gates pass.
- Shipping preset: `easy`, \(n=8\), 17-bit prime.
- Generic polynomial-time attack: 823,826 exact operations.
- Compact NTT route: 244 operations.
- Guessing: 0/200,000.
- Oracle results: bare 0/3, hinted 0/3, placebo 0/3.
- Answer size: 629 characters, 64 elements.

Track A is explicitly disclaimed because the protocols were subsequently broken by polynomial-time coefficient matching, as documented in the [cryptanalysis](https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.02964) of the [original paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.05457).

